@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:product] teams-text-extractable
In the Teams bot (`webhook_teams.ts` and `teams/`), translated text MUST be rendered with
`i18n._("<English text>", values)` on an `I18n` instance returned by `getBotI18n`
(`connectors/src/lib/bot/i18n.ts`), held in a binding named `i18n`, never with the global `i18n` of
`@lingui/core`. The first argument MUST be a string literal, which is both the message id and its
English text: `lingui extract` only collects literal ids passed to a callee named `i18n._`. Dynamic
parts MUST be named ICU placeholders (`{agentName}`) passed in `values`, never concatenated or
interpolated into the literal. Lingui macros (`@lingui/*/macro`) MUST NOT be imported: connectors
runs under `tsx`, which does not compile them.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:product] teams-user-text-translated
Text the Teams bot (`webhook_teams.ts` and `teams/`) writes for Teams users (messages, adaptive
card text, buttons, placeholders and errors) MUST be translated as specified by
`teams-text-extractable`. Content not authored by the bot (agent answers, agent and tool names, tool
labels from the Dust API, Teams data) MUST be interpolated untranslated through placeholders. The
`message` of an `Error` is diagnostic: it MAY stay English and MUST only reach users through the
placeholder of a translated sentence. Text sent to the Dust API or to models (message content,
content fragments) MUST NOT be translated.

@cc [owner:sfriquet,label:product] teams-text-in-workspace-locale
Teams bot text MUST be rendered with the `I18n` that `getTeamsI18n` (`teams/i18n.ts`) returns for
the connector of the Teams activity (`null` when the activity has none), whichever Teams user it is
written to. Outside `getTeamsI18n`, Teams bot production code MUST NOT pick a locale with
`getBotI18n` directly.
